# Copy to .env.local for local development.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is a prefix with consequences: everything carrying it is inlined
# into the client bundle and is readable by anyone who loads the page. Only put
# values here that are already public. Secrets belong in apps/api/.env, which the
# browser never sees.

# Where the API answers, and the same variable apps/web reads — one name for the
# API's location across both front ends, so a deployment configures it once. The
# console calls the API cross-origin with credentials — the httpOnly refresh
# cookie the API sets, and the bearer access token beside it — so it has to be on
# the API's CORS allowlist as ADMIN_ORIGIN in apps/api/.env; a mismatch fails
# staff sign-in at the preflight rather than as a wrong password.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3001
